Subject: [PATCH 4/4] End a block's lifetime with the one-operand CREVOKE
Upstream: CPython 3.13.7
Upstream-Archive: https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.7/Python-3.13.7.tgz
Upstream-SHA256: 6c9d80839cfa20024f34d9a6dd31ae2a9cd97ff5e980e969209746037a5153b2
Build-Variants: Capstone application on the virtual profile, PYMALLOC_SUBLET=ON (prepare-source.py --variant protected-virtual)
Depends-On: cpython-3.13.7-0003-blocks-as-sublet-lifetimes.patch
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

Patch 0003 ends a block with the two-operand CREVOKE of the capstone-sublet
bitstream (capstone_cap_revoke_child: the arena's child as parent, the block
as child). The processor model of the virtual profile takes the object alone
and refuses that encoding as an illegal instruction
(capstone/docs/design/virtual-capstone/isa.md). This patch replaces the two
revocations by capstone_cap_release, as the interpreter's patch 0014 does:

- pymalloc_free ends the block through the client's reference. CREVOKE
  faults when that reference is stale, so a double free stops there.
- pymalloc_realloc ends the client's child the same way before it issues
  one of the new length for a block that stays.

arena_life stays the parent every block is derived from. It is no longer an
operand of the revocation. Patch 0003 alone remains the bitstream's variant
(--variant protected).

--- a/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h
+++ b/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h
@@ -273,8 +273,8 @@
      * allocated arena.
      */
     uintptr_t address;
-    /* Sublet: the arena's child lifetime (CDERIVE), which carries MANAGE.
-     * Every block handed out is derived from it and revoked through it. */
+    /* Sublet: the arena's child lifetime (CDERIVE). Every block handed out
+     * is derived from it. A block ends through its own reference. */
     void *arena_life;
 
     /* Pool-aligned pointer to the next pool to be carved off. */
--- a/Objects/obmalloc.c
+++ b/Objects/obmalloc.c
@@ -2506,11 +2506,11 @@
     if (UNLIKELY(!address_in_range(state, p, pool))) {
         return 0;
     }
-    /* We allocated this address. End the client's lifetime of the block;
-       CREVOKE faults on a reference that is not a live block of this arena,
-       so a double or foreign free stops here. POOL_ADDR resolved the pool by
+    /* We allocated this address. End the client's lifetime of the block.
+       The client's reference is the only operand, and CREVOKE faults when it
+       is stale, so a double free stops here. POOL_ADDR resolved the pool by
        address, so obmalloc continues with its own pointer. */
-    capstone_cap_revoke_child(allarenas[pool->arenaindex].arena_life, p);
+    capstone_cap_release(p);
     p = (pymem_block *)pool + ((uintptr_t)p - (uintptr_t)pool);
 
     /* Link p to the start of the pool's freeblock list.  Since
@@ -2627,7 +2627,7 @@
         if (4 * nbytes > 3 * size) {
             /* It's the same, or shrinking and new/old > 3/4. The block stays;
                its client lifetime is replaced by one of the new length. */
-            capstone_cap_revoke_child(allarenas[pool->arenaindex].arena_life, p);
+            capstone_cap_release(p);
             *newptr_p = block_issue(
                 state, (pymem_block *)pool + ((uintptr_t)p - (uintptr_t)pool), nbytes);
             return 1;
